From 464df673f1d084f7c3d69993e13f4af7b3486e48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: issakakar <Issakakar@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:14:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] perf(editor): pick the search result shape by how it
 will be read

Measuring the consumers rather than the index changed the answer for one of
them. A query's membership stamps beat a Set when the number of probes is in
the same range as the number of matches, which is every hit test, brush and
eraser sweep. The viewport cull is the opposite: it probes every shape on the
page for a few hundred matches, so a small Set is a smaller table to hit
repeatedly than a page-sized id-to-slot map, and it goes back to
getShapeIdsInsideBounds.

SpatialQuery now also keeps a small result as a scannable list instead of
stamps. At the two or three matches a hit test returns that is a couple of
pointer compares, and an empty result answers has() with no work at all --
which is what closed a 25% regression in getShapeAtPoint.
